Execute Phase D5 only.

GOAL
Move a selected idea into the existing production workflow.

CREATE VIDEO
Show an editable project-creation summary:
- Title.
- Format and duration.
- Audience.
- Goal.
- Tone.
- Suggested prompt.
- Outline.
- Evidence links.
- Research gaps.

Require user acceptance before project creation.

Create the appropriate project type.
Do not overwrite an existing project.

DISTINGUISH EVIDENCE
Trend evidence supports topic selection.
It must not automatically become verified support for
the video's factual narration.

Preserve:
- Original idea ID.
- Evidence snapshot/reference.
- Generation provenance.
- User-edited prompt.
- Destination project ID.

MARK AS USED
Link the idea to its project.
Do not automatically dismiss all similar topics.

LONG-FORM
If full long-form rendering is unavailable:
Allow saving the outline or creating supported chapters,
but clearly explain the production limit.

SPENDING
Creating a draft project should not automatically start
image, narration, or render jobs.

Show the next generation steps and estimates separately.

TEST
Short idea → project → script → storyboard → real export.
Long idea → supported project/planning workflow.
Verify refresh, persistence, source distinctions, and no
unexpected generation charges.

ACCEPTANCE
A selected discovery idea becomes a real editable project
with traceable provenance and explicit user control.

Stop after D5.
